    {
      "id": "a0aa8d61a2bffd9ed46ab9a88e4ee095ef770358",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 978232874,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Is the intent to handle counted UTF-16 strings in which the count is in one byte order and the code elements are in another byte order?\n\nOr is this to support:\n\n- `ENC_UTF_16`, which is UTF-16 with a BOM required to specify the byte order;\n- `ENC_UTF_16LE`, which is little-endian UTF-16 (and where either a BOM is an error or must be little-endian);\n- `ENC_UTF_16BE`, which is big-endian UTF-16 (and where either a BOM is an error or must be big-endian)?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
